From 0b1240f3de01ad01f8fdb8412cc796c7a133a9f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:30:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 80/81] media: iris: Fix decoding with the Gen2 firmware of
 SM8450

The Gen2 firmware of the VPU 2.0 core (video-firmware 2.4, loaded on
SM8450 and SM8475) differs from the SM8550 firmware in two ways that
stop decoding:

- It answers HFI_CMD_RESUME with a payload (HFI_CMD_SETTINGS_CHANGE or
  HFI_CMD_DRAIN) with an information flag and does not resume. After
  the first source change no frame is ever decoded. The vendor driver
  (msm_vidc, waipio) sends the command without payload; with that the
  firmware resumes.
- It rejects the partial data buffer (HFI_BUFFER_PARTIAL_DATA), which
  the vendor driver never allocates.

Add a Gen2 firmware data variant for VPU 2.0 with these differences.
The shared Gen2 initializers move into a macro so both variants stay
in sync.

Tested on the Xiaomi 12T Pro (SM8475): 1080p HEVC and H.264 streams
decode bit-exactly (compared with ffmpeg) at about 165 frames/s.

Local Diting bring-up change, not submitted upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
